Classification:  Not classified

       Version:  4.3.5

          File:  IDDBKSYM ENTITIES
 Formal Public
   Identifiers:
                 Most recent version:
+//ISBN 0-933186::IBM//ENTITIES BookMaster Symbol Entity Declarations//EN

                 This version:
+//ISBN 0-933186::IBM//ENTITIES BookMaster Symbol Entity Declarations:4.2.3//EN

      Function:  These entity declarations support using the same names
                 for character entities that are defined by BookMaster
                 4.0.  In this version, the symbols resolve to the
                 same name but in the format used in the ISO character
                 entity declarations: entity name enclosed in square
                 brackets.

                 Each IBMIDDOC processing program, which requires other
                 values in these entity declarations must provide its
                 own copy of this file with those values specified.

Change History:  28Mar94 - Version 1.0 completed.
                 22Jun94 - Removed the SGML-related character entities
                           Added the character graphics entities
                 29Jun94 - Moved the ctq and otq entity definitions here.
                 24Mar95 - Changed the ctq/otq chars to the
                           same format as the rest of the chars.
                 06Jun96 - Made sure the char entities were SDATA entities.
                             including the box drawing entities.
                           Correct dso and dsc delimiter entities.
                  5Aug96 - V4.0.7: Add ENTVersion entity
                 25Feb97 - V4.2.0: Add mathast entity.
                 17Jul97 - V4.2.1: Changed replacement text to SGML-like entity reference.
                 16Jan98 - V4.2.2: Added shy entity
                 02Sep98 - V4.2.3: Added Euro entitites
                 03Sep98 -       : Added won entity
                 04Oct00 - V4.3.5: Added eserver_logo and eserver_logo_TM entities

=====================================================================-->

